<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">Berbice</h1><p class="st-meta">1627 CE – 1831 CE · capital New Amsterdam</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Dutch plantation colony on the Berbice river in Guyana, remembered above all for the great slave uprising of 1763.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1627 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-zeeland">Zeeland</a> merchant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-van-peere">Abraham van Peere</a> received a charter from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-west-india-company">Dutch West India Company</a> to settle the Berbice river. The colony began as a trading post at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-nassau-berbice">Fort Nassau</a> upriver and was run as a private patroonship by the van Peere family.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Berbice developed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> plantations worked by enslaved Africans. After a French raid in 1712, the colony was ransomed and from 1720 run by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/society-of-berbice">Society of Berbice</a>, a company of investors. In 1763 enslaved people led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuffy">Coffy</a> rose up, controlled most of the colony for nearly a year and were suppressed only with outside troops. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-amsterdam">New Amsterdam</a> later became the capital.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> occupied Berbice from 1796 and gained it formally in 1814. In 1831 it was merged with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/demerara-essequibo">Demerara-Essequibo</a> to form <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/british-guiana">British Guiana</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuffy">Coffy</a> is Guyana's national hero, and 23 February, the start of the uprising, is the country's Republic Day.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/berbice.jpg" alt="Berbice" width="320" height="209"><figcaption>Image: http://maps.bpl.org · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Berbice_in_1780.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1627 CE – 1831 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>New Amsterdam</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abraham van Peere, Coffy</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Dutch Reformed Church</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dutch, Berbice Creole Dutch</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Guyana</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Berbice colony</dd></dl></aside></div>
